Built-in catalog data
---------------------
The files in crates/ballistics-store/catalog/ hold calibers, bullets,
scopes, reticles, targets and animal drawings.

The separately licensed ChamberSim collection described below is an exception
to the descriptions of this project's independently compiled data.

  * Bullet, ammunition and scope figures are factual specifications compiled
    from the manufacturers' published product information (and, for a few
    entries, retailers' pages). Each entry names its source. Facts like
    these belong to no one; they are given as found, without warranty.
  * Reticle drawings are the project's own. Each is built by the project's
    own code from the subtension figures the maker publishes (spacings, line
    widths, hold-point positions), with the layout read from the maker's
    published picture; none is traced or copied from the makers' artwork.
    Each entry names its source and says which values were published and
    which were measured from the picture.
  * Animal drawings are the project's own, except the moose, which was
    generated with Recraft (recraft.ai) and adjusted by the project; the
    rights to it lie with the project under Recraft's paid-plan terms. The
    moose's hit area and rings follow Svenska Jägareförbundet's moose figure
    and the ring sizes in its rulebook (2025–28).
  * ISSF target dimensions follow the ISSF rules. The game guideline values
    (vital zones, minimum energies, sizes) are the project's own estimates;
    the Swedish ammunition classes summarise Naturvårdsverket's rules
    (NFS 2023:8), which are public law. Check the current rules.

The project's own parts of the catalog (the drawings, notes and guideline
values) are licensed under the same licences as the source code.

ChamberSim projectile data
-------------------------
The files in crates/ballistics-store/catalog/third-party/chambersim/ contain
selected, adapted records from the ChamberSim Reloaded project database:
https://github.com/Schildkroet/ChamberSim-Reloaded

This data collection is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Credit: ChamberSim Reloaded project database. The upstream license declaration,
source revision, file hashes and selection decisions are retained with the data.
Each imported record carries its attribution and a link to the source record.

Changes: selected component records, renamed fields and converted grains to
grams. Source lengths and uncertainty descriptions are retained in notes;
the active length field remains unknown. BCs were copied without fitting or
independent verification. Construction, lead-free status and expansion limits
were not established by the import. Possible existing matches and packaging
duplicates were excluded.

